        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "OpenCode's LSP feature requires a language server to be installed and configured for the language(s) in your project. The project here is Go-based, so it needs `gopls` to be available.\n\nA few common reasons LSP shows as empty:\n\n1. **No language server installed** — for Go, `gopls` needs to be on your `$PATH`. Check with:\n   ```sh\n   which gopls\n   ```\n   Install if missing:\n   ```sh\n   go install golang.org/x/tools/gopls@latest\n   ```\n\n2. **OpenCode config has no LSP entries** — OpenCode may need explicit LSP configuration. Check `~/.config/opencode/config.json` for an `lsp` section.\n\n3. **No `go.work` or the module path is unresolvable** — OpenCode might not detect the Go module if you're opening a subdirectory (`bridge/`) rather than the workspace root.\n\n4. **Binary not found at session start** — LSP servers are detected at launch; if `gopls` wasn't on `$PATH` when OpenCode started, it won't show up.\n\nWhich of these would you like me to investigate further?",
